[[Carlos Alcaraz]] is the defending champion. {{cite news |last=Jurejko |first=Jonathan |url= https://www.bbc.com/sport/tennis/articles/c8xrpd5jeveo|title=Alcaraz edges Sinner trilogy to win US Open |date=7 September 2025 |work=BBC Sport |accessdate=8 September 2025}} This will mark his first singles appearance in over four months, following a wrist injury he suffered at the [[2026 Barcelona Open Banc Sabadell – Singles|Barcelona Open]]. {{cite web |last1=Dedovic |first1=Sead |title=Carlos Alcaraz chooses in-form star for important practice before US Open return |url=https://www.tennisworldusa.org/tennis/news/Carlos_Alcaraz/169066/carlos-alcaraz-chooses-inform-star-for-important-practice-before-us-open-return/ |website=Tennis World USA |access-date=26 August 2026 |language=en |date=25 August 2026}} 

[[Novak Djokovic]]'s first-round defeat to [[Mariano Navone]] marked only his third career loss in the opening round of a [[Grand Slam (tennis)#Tournaments|major]], his first opening-round loss at the [[US Open (tennis)|US Open]], and his earliest loss at a major since the [[2006 Australian Open – Men's singles|2006 Australian Open]]. {{Cite web | title = Mariano Navone stuns physically ailing Novak Djokovic at US Open | publisher = ATP Tour, Inc. | date = 31 August 2026 | url = https://www.atptour.com/en/news/djokovic-navone-us-open-2026-r1 | accessdate = 31 August 2026}} This marked the first time that none of the [[Big Three (tennis)|Big Three]] reached the second round of a major since the [[2003 French Open – Men's singles|2003 French Open]]. {{Cite web | title = Novak Djokovic's US Open exit ends remarkable Big Three Grand Slam streak | publisher = Sportstar | date = 31 August 2026 | url = https://sportstar.thehindu.com/tennis/novak-djokovic-us-open-exit-big-three-streak-2003-french-open/article71409707.ece | accessdate = 31 August 2026}} 

This tournament marked the first absence from a major of current [[List of ATP number 1 ranked singles players|world No. 1]] [[Jannik Sinner]] since the [[2019 Wimbledon Championships – Men's singles|2019 Wimbledon Championships]]. {{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/tennis/articles/cvgw2qg3e70o|title=Injured Sinner & Draper withdraw from US Open|publisher=[[BBC Sport]]|last=Jurejko|first=Jonathan|date=August 21, 2026|access-date=August 23, 2026}} 

This tournament will mark the final major appearances of [[2016 US Open – Men's singles|2016]] champion, three-time major champion and former world No. 3 [[Stan Wawrinka]] and former world No. 6 [[Gaël Monfils]]. {{cite web |title= Wawrinka given late wildcard for US Open farewell |url= https://www.bbc.com/sport/tennis/articles/cvgye2w5x20o |website=BBC Sport |accessdate=26 August 2026 |date=26 August 2026}} 

